*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# The workflow and the compose file are read by Linux tooling, and both carry shell inside
# them. A Windows clone committing CRLF would put a \r at the end of every line of the
# deploy step's `run: |` block, so the VM would be asked to `git checkout dev\r` - which
# fails in a way that reads as a git problem rather than a line-ending one.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Not text. Without this, a .gitattributes `text=auto` or a Windows checkout could rewrite
# bytes inside a FlatBuffer or protobuf container and corrupt a model with no visible diff.
*.tflite binary
*.task binary
*.onnx binary
*.wasm binary
